IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), s 23.3(6) to (9): the end of the benefits for a person who
-- cares for a critically ill adult. Piece ei2. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws
-- consolidation current to 2026-09-30. Seat: the person who cares for the adult and claims the benefit.
--
-- Section 23.3 opens at line 646 (piece ei1 encodes subsections (1) to (5): who qualifies, the certificate,
-- the period in subsection (3), the exception, the deferral of the waiting period). This module takes the
-- period of subsection (3) as an input and encodes only what is left: (6) to (9).
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld), stated once, in the layer-1 rule that carries them:
--   (6)  the claimants jointly hold a power to divide the weeks as they agree; the Commission is liable to pay
--        the weeks as divided, and, if they cannot agree, the prescribed rules divide them (reg 41.6, piece er3);
--   (8)  the Commission holds a privilege not to pay compassionate care benefits in respect of the adult for that
--        period, and the claimant has no claim to them;
--   (9)  the Commission is empowered (and, by "shall", bound) to reduce or eliminate; the claimant is liable to
--        have the benefits reduced or eliminated as prescribed.

§ `Section 23.3(6) and (7) - dividing the weeks between claimants`

-- The figure the text states: 15 weeks. Both subsections use it, so it is carried once.
-- src:671 | (6) If a claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and another claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.062 in respect of the same adult, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 152.062 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 15 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by those claimants. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
-- src:673 | (7) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same adult, a claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and another claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 152.062, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 152.062 that may be divided between them must not exceed 15 weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.3(6), s 23.3(7) (src:671) (src:673)
`s 23.3(6) and (7) the most weeks that may be divided between claimants` MEANS 15

-- "If a claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and another claimant makes a claim for benefits
-- under this section or section 152.062 in respect of the same adult, any remaining weeks of benefits payable
-- ... up to a maximum of 15 weeks, may be divided". The remaining weeks are the number of weeks of benefits
-- still payable under this section, under section 152.062 or under both; the rule gives how many of them may
-- be divided. If the condition does not hold the section does not let any weeks be divided: 0.
-- src:670 | Division of weeks of benefits
-- src:671 | (6) If a claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and another claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.062 in respect of the same adult, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 152.062 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 15 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by those claimants. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.3(6) (src:670-671)
GIVEN `a claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 23.3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another claimant makes a claim under section 23.3 or 152.062 in respect of the same adult` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the remaining weeks of benefits payable under section 23.3, under section 152.062 or under both` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23.3(6) the number of remaining weeks that may be divided` IS
    IF     `a claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 23.3`
       AND `another claimant makes a claim under section 23.3 or 152.062 in respect of the same adult`
    THEN IF `the remaining weeks of benefits payable under section 23.3, under section 152.062 or under both` AT MOST `s 23.3(6) and (7) the most weeks that may be divided between claimants`
         THEN `the remaining weeks of benefits payable under section 23.3, under section 152.062 or under both`
         ELSE `s 23.3(6) and (7) the most weeks that may be divided between claimants`
    ELSE 0

-- "... may be divided in the manner agreed to by those claimants. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are
-- to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules." "If they cannot agree" is read as "if they have not agreed" (fork ei2-F1). The prescribed rules are reg 41.6 (out of range:
-- Regulations s 41.6, piece er3); here only which of the two ways governs is decided.
-- src:671 | (6) If a claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and another claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.062 in respect of the same adult, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 152.062 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 15 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by those claimants. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.3(6) (src:671)
GIVEN `the claimants have agreed how to divide the weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `ei2 Way of dividing the weeks`
DECIDE `s 23.3(6) the way the remaining weeks are divided` IS
    IF `the claimants have agreed how to divide the weeks`
    THEN `ei2 divided in the manner the claimants agreed`
    ELSE `ei2 divided in accordance with the prescribed rules`

-- "(7) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same adult, a claimant makes a claim for benefits under this
-- section and another claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 152.062, the total number of weeks of
-- benefits payable under this section and section 152.062 that may be divided between them must not exceed 15
-- weeks." The rule tests a proposed total against the ceiling; NOTHING when the subsection does not apply,
-- because it then says nothing about the total.
-- src:672 | Maximum divisible number of weeks
-- src:673 | (7) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same adult, a claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and another claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 152.062, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 152.062 that may be divided between them must not exceed 15 weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.3(7) (src:672-673)
GIVEN `a claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 23.3 in respect of an adult` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 152.062 in respect of the same adult` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total number of weeks under section 23.3 and section 152.062 that are divided between them` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.3(7) the total number of weeks divided is within the ceiling` IS
    IF     `a claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 23.3 in respect of an adult`
       AND `another claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 152.062 in respect of the same adult`
    THEN JUST (`the total number of weeks under section 23.3 and section 152.062 that are divided between them` AT MOST `s 23.3(6) and (7) the most weeks that may be divided between claimants`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 23.3(8) - the limitation on compassionate care benefits`

-- "(8) Benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable in respect of an adult during the period referred to
-- in subsection (3) or 152.062(3) that is established in respect of that adult." Sections 23.1 and 152.06 are
-- the compassionate care benefits, the keel's reason `care or support of a family member`. The period is
-- established by s 23.3(3) (out of range: section 23.3(3), piece ei1) or s 152.062(3) (out of range: section
-- 152.062(3), piece ei5): it is an input, a `Period of days`, and the week is identified by its Sunday.
-- src:674 | Limitation — compassionate care benefits
-- src:675 | (8) Benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable in respect of an adult during the period referred to in subsection (3) or 152.062(3) that is established in respect of that adult.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.3(8) (src:674-675)
GIVEN `the reason for the benefits claimed` IS A `Reason for benefits`
      `the benefits are claimed in respect of the adult for whom the period was established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Sunday of the week for which the benefits are claimed` IS A DATE
      `the period referred to in subsection 23.3(3) or 152.062(3) established in respect of the adult` IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.3(8) benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable` IF
        `the reason for the benefits claimed` EQUALS `care or support of a family member`
    AND `the benefits are claimed in respect of the adult for whom the period was established`
    AND `the day` `the Sunday of the week for which the benefits are claimed` `falls within` `the period referred to in subsection 23.3(3) or 152.062(3) established in respect of the adult`

§ `Section 23.3(9) - benefits under a provincial law`

-- "(9) When benefits are payable to a claimant for the reasons set out in this section and any allowances, money or
-- other benefits are payable to the claimant under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same
-- reasons, the benefits payable to the claimant under this section shall be reduced or eliminated as prescribed."
-- Whether a payment under a provincial law is for "the same or substantially the same reasons" is a judgment
-- the text hands to whoever applies it; it is a BOOLEAN input. How much the reduction is, is "as prescribed":
-- no regulation among the inputs prescribes it for section 23.3 (see NOTES.md, "Cross-references out of my
-- ranges"), so the rule says only that the reduction or elimination applies.
-- src:676 | Limitation
-- src:677 | (9) When benefits are payable to a claimant for the reasons set out in this section and any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same reasons, the benefits payable to the claimant under this section shall be reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.3(9) (src:676-677)
GIVEN `benefits are payable to the claimant for the reasons set out in section 23.3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are payable for the same or substantially the same reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.3(9) the benefits payable under section 23.3 are to be reduced or eliminated as prescribed` IF
        `benefits are payable to the claimant for the reasons set out in section 23.3`
    AND `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant under a provincial law`
    AND `they are payable for the same or substantially the same reasons`
